# @epistemologic/property/verdict_is_content_addressed — the
# substrate-decl that lifts `crystal.derived_predicates` from
# "audit trail of what was verified" to "memoizable cache by
# construction." N1 TICK 1 landing per Reed's RED tick `22dba0d`
# and Taut scout report on incremental compilation (this session).
#
# THE CLAIM: `verdict(spec_oid, target_oid, inputs_oid) -> verdict`
# IS a TOTAL FUNCTION of its input OIDs. Same inputs -> same
# verdict, always, trivially. Memoization is valid by construction
# (no invalidation logic required beyond checking whether the input
# OID triple has changed).
#
# Interpretation B canonical per Seam pre-review
# `docs/audits/2026-07-06-seam-arc-4-sub-arc-a-pre-review.md` §1:
# narrative ABOVE `---`; `in` clauses + typed declarations BELOW.
#
# === Recognition #43 grounding (mirror IS content-addressed build system) ===
#
# THE OPERATIONAL CONSEQUENCE OF RECOGNITION #43 AT VERDICT ALTITUDE.
#
# Per `[[architecture-mirror-as-content-addressed-build-system]]`
# (#43 LANDED at M6 TICK 1 `884f433`): mirror has every Bazel /
# Buck2 / Nix / Shake primitive declared at substrate altitude;
# mosaic.mirror IS the build shard. Recognition #43 promoted on
# the strength of `partial(opacity_map)` being genuinely sharper
# than every canon's binary verdict.
#
# This shard is the operational consequence of #43 at the verdict
# altitude: when mirror IS a content-addressed build system, then
# verdicts issued by the kintsugi loop over that build system MUST
# themselves be content-addressed. The predicate names the
# invariant that makes verdict-caching valid by construction rather
# than by ad-hoc invalidation logic. Every Bazel / Buck2 / Nix
# lineage canon (Dolstra 2006 purely-functional deployment; Bazel
# REAPI ActionCache; Buck2 dep graph) grounds a content-addressed
# verdict/action-cache surface; this shard declares the mirror-
# altitude form as substrate primitive.
#
# === The total-function invariant ===
#
# The predicate signature
#
#   verdict_is_content_addressed(spec_oid, target_oid, inputs_oid)
#     -> verdict { \ }
#
# discharges the claim that:
#
#   verdict = f(spec_oid, target_oid, inputs_oid)
#
# is a total function of its three OID inputs. "Total function"
# means: defined on every triple of valid OIDs; single-valued (same
# inputs -> same verdict); purely-functional (referentially
# transparent, no side channel, no clock, no environment). This is
# a purely functional referentially transparent map from the
# (spec, target, inputs) OID triple to a verdict OID.
#
# The three OID parameters:
#
#   - `spec_oid: oid` — the content-address of the property
#     specification (the shard declaring the predicate whose verdict
#     we cache); resolved through @mirror/store.
#   - `target_oid: oid` — the content-address of the object under
#     verdict (the artifact / crystal / splinter the predicate is
#     evaluated against); resolved through @mirror/store.
#   - `inputs_oid: oid` — the content-address of the composed input
#     bundle (dependency closure OIDs, environment OIDs, ancestor
#     verdicts folded in); the canonical hash of the inputs that
#     participated in producing the verdict. Distinct from
#     target_oid because inputs include the transitive dependency
#     closure the target references, not just the target's own bytes.
#
# The three OIDs together are the complete addressing of a verdict.
# Nothing else participates. No clock, no environment variable, no
# ambient state. If the substrate observes the same triple twice,
# it MUST issue the same verdict — this is not a policy claim but a
# substrate-decl invariant discharged by content-addressing at
# every layer beneath (per @mirror/store OID discipline).
#
# === The memoization-by-construction consequence ===
#
# When verdict is a total function of input OIDs, memoization is
# VALID BY CONSTRUCTION. No invalidation logic is required beyond
# checking whether the input OID triple has changed. A cache lookup
# keyed on `(spec_oid, target_oid, inputs_oid)` either returns the
# previously-issued verdict (a cache hit; verdict re-issue is
# skipped) OR returns the sentinel `miss` (the substrate must run
# the kintsugi loop to issue a fresh verdict, then write it to the
# cache under the same key).
#
# Consequence for the `crystal.derived_predicates` carrier at
# `shards/mirror/store/crystal.mirror` lines 344-368: the field was
# landed as an audit-trail of what the kintsugi loop verified during
# settlement (`derived_predicates: [property_verdict]`). This
# predicate lifts it to a memoizable cache by construction — the
# `[property_verdict]` list IS the substrate-decl'd cache entries;
# each `property_verdict = { verdict, where: location }` becomes a
# key/value pair in the content-addressed verdict cache once the
# location keys off the input OID triple. Trivially cacheable
# because content-addressed. No invalidation heuristic; no
# generational counter; no mtime probe.
#
# === @mirror/store composition ===
#
# This predicate composes with `@mirror/store` (per
# `shards/mirror/store.mirror` §"Apache-2.0 rock-solid floor
# discipline" + §"Non-negotiable v0 invariants"): the store
# provides `oid`, `walk`, `read`, `write`, `verify` primitives
# whose immutability-under-hash + purely-functional-composition
# invariants ground this predicate's total-function claim.
#
# Store invariant (1) — immutability-under-hash — grounds the
# "same input OID triple always addresses the same bytes"
# assumption: because `OID = BLAKE3(content)` by construction, the
# spec_oid / target_oid / inputs_oid are stable identifiers whose
# byte-content cannot mutate under the identifier.
#
# Store invariant (2) — composition is purely-functional — grounds
# the "same triple -> same verdict" claim: verdict issuance IS a
# composition of prisms acting on stored OIDs; therefore the output
# is a total function of the inputs.
#
# Together the two @mirror/store invariants ARE the substrate-
# altitude witnesses that this predicate is well-formed at declaration
# altitude. No further arithmetic is needed to justify the
# content-addressing claim: it inherits from the store.
#
# The action-hash -> OID map (REAPI ActionCache surface;
# `@mirror/store/action_cache` forward-promised at M6 tick 3 per
# `shards/mirror/store.mirror` §"Bazel REAPI floor decomposition")
# is the natural home for the verdict cache at store altitude. This
# predicate declares the semantic invariant; the action_cache sub-
# prism will house the concrete `record` / `lookup` actions keyed
# by verdict-triples (N2 forward-promise below).
#
# === @fate hinge composition (verdicts EMERGE from runtime) ===
#
# Per Recognition #58 ([[architecture-fate-is-optical-inference]];
# LANDED 2026-06-11 via Seam adversarial review): Fate inference IS
# 5-layer D²NN + active Fabry-Perot resonator + Reck/Clements
# unitary mesh. Per the @fate substrate-decl at `shards/fate.mirror`
# (2026-06-30 05:24, 42.1KB): @fate IS the hinge between runtime
# and compiletime — the constrained-inference operator whose dice-
# roll within the restricted state space produces verdicts at
# runtime that this shard names content-addressed at compiletime.
#
# Verdicts EMERGE from Fate optical inference at runtime; this
# predicate ANCHORS the compiletime/runtime hinge by declaring that
# whatever verdict Fate issues for a given `(spec_oid, target_oid,
# inputs_oid)` triple IS a total function of that triple. The
# runtime substrate (D²NN + Fabry-Perot + unitary mesh) supplies
# the actual inference arithmetic; the substrate-decl'd hinge at
# `@fate` binds runtime arithmetic to the compiletime declaration.
# This predicate names the invariant Fate must honor across the
# hinge — the same input triple must produce the same output
# verdict, so that the verdict may be cached across both
# compiletime substrate-decl resolution and runtime execution.
#
# The compiletime + runtime bilateral discipline per @fate
# ("Alex's BILATERAL correction" per `shards/fate.mirror`): the
# same inferential machinery operates at substrate-decl resolution
# time (picking among morphism candidates / resolving `\` typed-gap
# holes during static analysis) AND at runtime (driving actual
# data flow decisions as gen_prisms execute). This predicate's
# content-addressed invariant covers BOTH altitudes: a compile-time
# @fate crystal keyed by (spec, target, inputs) OIDs is memoization
# for the compiletime pass; a runtime @fate crystal keyed by the
# same triple is memoization for the runtime pass; both keys index
# the same content-addressed cache.
#
# === mosaic-store-cache-invariants spec grounding ===
#
# Per `docs/specs/mosaic-store-cache-invariants.md` (Mara
# 2026-06-28, 2016 lines): §9.2 forward-promises 8 bilateral shard
# pairs at `@epistemologic/property/*` + `@kintsugi/fracture/*`
# altitudes; none had landed at the time the spec was authored.
# This shard is one of them landing — the declarative half of the
# verdict/content-addressing bilateral pair. The operational half
# at `@kintsugi/fracture/verdict_cache_miss` (or equivalent naming)
# is forward-promised as the fracture-side surface for the case
# where the cache lookup returns `miss` and the kintsugi loop must
# re-issue the verdict.
#
# The mosaic-store-cache-invariants spec grounds the broader cache
# invariant discipline at store altitude; this shard grounds the
# specific verdict-altitude invariant that authorizes the cache
# path for property verdicts.
#
# === Operational target: the 13-minute pre-commit hook ===
#
# Business context (Taut scout report, this session): the pre-
# commit hook takes ~13 minutes because `cmd_kintsugi_spec` at
# `bootstrap/src/lib.rs:~1189` walks every target on every
# invocation and spawns `cargo <check>` cold each time. Zero
# cross-invocation cache; zero per-target result memoization.
#
# This shard is the substrate-decl that authorizes memoization to
# become the standard path. When this predicate lands, the
# kintsugi loop MAY consult a content-addressed verdict cache
# keyed by `(spec_oid, target_oid, inputs_oid)` before dispatching
# cargo. On cache hit: skip cargo; re-emit the cached verdict.
# On cache miss: run cargo, record the verdict at the triple's
# key, emit. The hook overhead falls from ~13 minutes to seconds
# on the second invocation because incremental verdict caching
# is now valid by construction.
#
# The operational target grounds the substrate-decl in its
# consumer discipline; without a landed consumer path the
# predicate is analytical only. Recognition #43 supplies the
# principled ancestor; the pre-commit hook supplies the
# empirical pull.
#
# === N-cascade forward-promises ===
#
# This shard is N1 TICK 1 of the N-cascade (incremental verdict
# cache + kintsugi-IS-commit). Downstream N-cascade ticks:
#
#   - N2: `cache_read` + `cache_write` at `@mirror/store` keyed on
#         `(spec_oid, target_oid, inputs_oid) -> verdict`. The
#         concrete cache-lookup + cache-write actions that
#         operationalize this predicate's memoization invariant.
#         The natural next tick following this landing.
#
#   - N3: Rust wiring at `bootstrap/src/lib.rs:~1189` —
#         `cmd_kintsugi_spec` consults the verdict cache before
#         dispatching cargo. Cache hit: skip cargo, emit cached
#         verdict. Cache miss: run cargo, record verdict.
#
#   - N4: reverse closure `impacted_by(oid) -> [oid]` at
#         `@mirror/store`. When an OID changes, the reverse-
#         closure walk names every downstream OID whose cached
#         verdict may be affected. Composes with N2 cache_read to
#         invalidate exactly the impacted verdict entries.
#
#   - N5: `@kintsugi/store/git commit-as-fold` — `mirror kintsugi
#         --commit` IS `git commit` at git-projection altitude.
#         Every commit is a fold over the verdict cache; every
#         reverse-closure walk is a rebase over the fold. The
#         terminal tick of the N-cascade at kintsugi-projection
#         altitude.
#
# The N-cascade grounds this predicate as the anchor point for the
# incremental verdict discipline. Each N-tick composes downstream
# of this one; nothing downstream is valid without this predicate
# declaring the total-function invariant that authorizes the whole
# cache path.
#
