# === verdict_is_content_addressed predicate (declarative half) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING PREDICATE. Returns verdict that
# `verdict = f(spec_oid, target_oid, inputs_oid)` is a total
# function of its three OID inputs — same triple -> same verdict,
# always. Content-addressing at every layer beneath (per
# @mirror/store OID discipline invariants (1) immutability-under-
# hash + (2) composition is purely-functional) grounds the total-
# function claim as substrate-decl invariant.
#
# The three OID parameters name the complete addressing of a
# verdict: `spec_oid` names the predicate specification; `target_oid`
# names the object under verdict; `inputs_oid` names the composed
# input bundle (dependency closure + environment + ancestor
# verdicts folded in). No clock; no ambient state; no side channel.
#
# Consequence: memoization is VALID BY CONSTRUCTION. A cache
# lookup keyed on `(spec_oid, target_oid, inputs_oid)` either
# returns the previously-issued verdict (hit; skip re-issue) or
# the sentinel `miss` (run kintsugi loop, re-issue, write to
# cache). No invalidation heuristic; no generational counter; no
# mtime probe. The predicate declares the invariant; N2's
# cache_read + cache_write actions operationalize it; N3's Rust
# wiring consumes the cache at the pre-commit hook; N4's reverse-
# closure walks invalidate exactly the impacted entries; N5's
# commit-as-fold projects the whole cascade at git altitude.
#
# Body discharges as obligation block (`\`) — realisation
# dispatches through the substrate; the shard declares the
# contract only. The concrete verdict-issuance arithmetic lives
# in the kintsugi loop at @fate runtime altitude; the concrete
# cache actions live at @mirror/store/action_cache (N2 forward-
# promised).
verdict_is_content_addressed(spec_oid: oid, target_oid: oid, inputs_oid: oid)
  -> verdict { \ }

out @epistemologic/property/verdict_is_content_addressed
out verdict_is_content_addressed
